# ── Personal job-search data — NEVER in this repo ────────────────────────────
# This platform is shared by more than one person. Each user's CV, pipeline, salary bands,
# rejections and interview debriefs live in $PROFILE_DIR, OUTSIDE this repo. A shared private
# repo is not isolation: committing any of this makes it permanently visible to everyone else
# with access. `test_profile.py::test_no_profile_dir_content_is_tracked_by_git` enforces it.
profile.json
profiles/*.json
!profiles/_template.json
!profiles/_fixtures/*.json
# The CI fixture profile. `profile.json` above has no leading slash, so it matches at ANY
# depth and silently swallowed this file: CI then found the fixture's notes but no profile,
# the RAG gate reported SKIPPED, and the step passed having asserted nothing — the exact
# defect that step exists to prevent. Contains no personal data; see the file's _comment.
# `test_rag_cli.py::test_ci_fixture_profile_is_tracked_by_git` enforces that it stays tracked.
!profiles/_fixtures/rag_demo/profile.json
# `positions/*`, NOT `positions/` — git cannot re-include anything inside an EXCLUDED
# DIRECTORY, so the `!` lines below are dead if the directory itself is excluded. That is
# why the layout template silently failed to ship on the first attempt.
positions/*
# The layout template MUST ship, or a new user clones a platform whose per-position
# structure is undocumented. It contains no personal data.
!positions/_template/
job-tracking/
cv.md
cv_*.md
cv*.pdf
CV_*.pdf
CV_*.md
_drafts/
**/_drafts/

# ── Secrets and private config ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
ats_targets.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.mcp.json

